<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chinese Civil War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927–1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chinese Civil War was fought between the Nationalist government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a>, in two phases from 1927 to 1937 and from 1945 to 1949, interrupted by the war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. The Communists under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> won and proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> in October 1949, while the Nationalists withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war.jpg" alt="Chinese Civil War" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Siping03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
